    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d581">

                <pb facs="0821" n="741" sameAs="frus:frus1936v01/pg741"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">841.6363/425</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the British Ambassador</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Lindsay</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1936-07-20">July 20, 1936</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Excellency</hi>: Reference is made to your note of
                    July 6th, requesting confirmation that the Government of the United States does
                    in fact regard Great Britain as a reciprocal country under the Mineral Leasing
                    Act of 1920.</p>
                <p>I have the honor to inform you that the Department of the Interior is now
                    prepared to recognize Great Britain as a reciprocal country under the Mineral
                    Leasing Act of 1920. A copy of the letter from the Acting Secretary of the
                    Interior in this connection is enclosed.<anchor n="11" xml:id="d581-f1"/>
                </p>
                <p>Accept [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Cordell Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
